I lost the rest, sadly enough, but obied no conducts that i now of.  I never
polyed any objects.  But I was polymorphed numerous times in the beginning,
and that was a bit of fun.  Hiding out in the gnomish mines, in a small
house waiting to revert to normal form.   3 times I hid in locked rooms
waiting for revert back, except the second time, when I was poly'd into a
master mindflayer, and I ran around killing stuff instead.  The first time
left be as a gelatinous cube, and the third as an orc mummy.   I'm not sure
how I sirvived hose incitents, but they would prove to be the closest I came
to death until running uop agianst Pestilence in the end game.

Anyway I started, and made my way down to about level 10.  I moved slowly,
and it was pretty unadventful up to that point, then I ran into the mines.
made my way down to the level past the minetown and found an old bones
level, which had a whole lot of nothing.  (as you can tell from the score
board, this copy of nethack was onloy rescently installed on my new
computer).  But what the bones statue did have was a ring ot polymorph and
polymorph control, whchi became useful later for getting some of the more
seless intrinsics, that I would've gotten anyway when I was crowned.

A quick dip, early gave me Excalibur, which would turn out ot be a faithful
companian for the remander of the game.  A magic lamp from the lighting shop
gave me +2 GDSM.  A co-aligned alter before back in the dungeins of doom,
and a found bag of tricks left me with Mojo.   Sokoban was a joke, and left
me with the "oR.  As well the =oSD came early, but proved to be nothing as 5
were found at various points in the dame.  Same with =oC.  4 of those were
found at various points along the way.  As well as backup "oR.   Bags of
holding were also not in short supply.

Fort Ludous gave me a naked AC of 0.  (that last point of protection was
very expensive). after the money was lugged back down to the gnomish mines.
I then set up base ni the barracks of fort ludious, as well as in a now
co-aligned temple that was in the level below the one containing the portal.

I milled around the dungeons of doom for a long time, until I was able to
finally get boots of levitation, and uncursing them lead me over Medusa's
little lake.  Kill the lady and proceded to the castle.  Decided to hold
off, and went back to do the quest.  Made short work of that, as the Valk
quest is a bit of a joke.

The most useful bit of information I foundon this newsgroup was the use of
the ring of conflict.  I had never before realized how great an item it is
until I got to the castle.  I didn't know the song, so I just blasted open
the door with awand of striking and put on the ring.  Then I blindfolded
myself and waited.  I watched as all of the monsters in the courtyard killed
each other off, leaving me free to levetate over the moat (after using cone
of cold and block off attacks from ;'s) and collect what was in there.  the
armoury had a +1 Hawaiian shirt, and the wand of wishing quickly lead to
gauntlets of power, and speed boots.  the first pair of speed boots were
lost to over-enchantment(a good example of what happens when you play
nethack when you are tired, and not paying attention) and I wished for
another pair.  The wand had two wishes left, and I decided to leave them.
One for a helm of opposite alignment for the endgame, if I didn't need it
before then, but the other two were foing to be for charging scrolls, or
wands of death to keep of the onslaught in the endgame.

Vlad's tower was easy enough with an AC of -27, MR and reflection.  Since I
wasn't going two-weapon I decided to go with the "oLS and the shield of
reflection.  I then made it down to the vobration square and marked it.  I
hadn't bought the candles yet, for the following reason.  I figued they
aren't going anywhere.  As I went through each level, after I got a pick
axe, I had carved out the ascension path I would have to take after.  So I
decide to to a practise run. Obviously there was no Rodney, but it turned
uot to be a good idea.  (up to this point, the closest I had come top
ascension was getting the amulet, only to be killed by Rodney in Jublix's
layer, after being teleported back to jublis level twice)

Went to the stash, got a bag of holding ready, containing scrolls of gold
detection, and potions of confusion and booze.  Brought it up to level 1.
Left it next o the stairs on an Elbereth square.  Got the candles, and went
back the Rodney's tower.  While ascending the tower, I was hit my master
mind flayer, resulting in amnesia.  (boo)  The wand of death killed rodney,
and i did the ascension run.

The sanctum was easy enough with a ring of conflict and the wand of death.
Got the amulet, and quickly quaffed a potion of gain level to get out of the
sanctum.  Started the Ascension.  This is when I noticed I was starting to
get very lucky.  I was sent backwards numerous times, but saw Rodney only
once, before i got back to the castle.  Again, easly killed by the wand of
death.  The secong blessed charging scroll left me with a wand thast had 8
charges, which turned out to be enough to hnlde Rodeny all the way to the
the Astral Plane.  When up to the castle level, it turned out that the RGN
had some ticks left up its sleeve.  It had generated a gremlin on the moat
around the castle, and the bottom half of the castle level map was covered
in little '1s' from the warning the orb of heaviness gave me.  I lost one
intrinsic trying to get through them all to the other side.  I still don't
know what it was, to be honest.

Got to level one after running into Rodney numerous times, in the dungeons.
Never doble teamed, though he was always dead by wand the turn after he
showed up.  Navagating the forgotten levels in the maze was easy enough, I
just had to folow the cut out walls I had made.  The forgotton dungeon
levels were also easy enough.

The elemental planes were surprisingly easy.  gold detection made it easy as
well as conflict.  Though the air elemental plane loked like it was going to
get dicy, but most o f the time the elementals left me alone as they were
attacking something else entirely.

On to the astral plane.  I took the ring off before goign in, thinking the
pet would help.  Pestilece made short work of him, and I put the ring back
on when a crowd started showing up.  The aligned priest that were there
started summoning insects, which I happily used as a shield and made my way
closer. There were some close sickness incidences becauise of the Pestilence
attacks.  I charged another empty wand of death to deal with him.

I had picked out the proper room first try, and made it to the alter.  It
was very close, you will notice in my intrinsics that I sick from illness at
the time of ascension.

All in all, one of the sloppiest first ascensinos I;ve had the pleasrure of
reading.

